WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.720
Love it, or hate it.

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:04.420
There’s no question that the Cybertruck
has divided opinions.

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.170
“It’s gonna be a Lamborghini.

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:07.990
It’s gonna cost too much.

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:10.870
There’s gonna be a gigantic battery.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:14.440
I’m calling it a toy for Elon fanboys.”

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:18.289
Even Tesla’s own design team had mixed feelings
about the Cybertruck.

00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:22.820
Tesla’s chief designer Franz von Holzhausen
said in Walter Isaacson’s biography of Elon

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:26.130
Musk: “A majority of people in this studio
hated it.”

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.439
“They were like, ‘You can’t be serious.’”

00:00:28.439 --> 00:00:30.280
Elon was serious.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.950
He felt they had played it safe with the look
of the Model Y

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:36.270
And wanted to make a bold statement with the
Cybertruck.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:42.230
Once in every ten years, once in awhile, a
really unusual product special product comes

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.480
along.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:47.410
We’ll remember those special moments.

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:48.410
Innovation can be shocking.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:49.910
New designs can be unsettling

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:51.840
Remember when people laughed at AirPods?

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.100
Elon’s son Saxon once asked: “Why doesn’t
the future look like the future?”

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.650
That really resonated with Elon.

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:04.339
Finally, the future will look like the future.

00:01:04.339 --> 00:01:08.550
His vision for a forward-looking design was
inspired by the Lotus Esprit from the James

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:13.530
Bond film 'The Spy Who Loved Me,' a car he
admired so much that he bought it for $1 million

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:17.420
and gave it a place of honor in Tesla's design
studio.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.979
And the Cybertruck’s engineering seemed
to naturally call for a futuristic look.

00:01:21.979 --> 00:01:26.460
The vehicle is made from the same stainless
steel used in SpaceX’s Starship, so it’s

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:29.020
certainly tough enough for terrestrial travel.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:33.340
The body panels used in cars are traditionally
made out of aluminum or steel alloys because

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:34.780
of their ease of use and cost-effectiveness.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:40.970
However, Elon wondered whether another material
would be better for a durable, high-performance

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:42.329
electric truck.

00:01:42.329 --> 00:01:46.939
This is an example of first principles thinking
- challenging the status quo, breaking down

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:49.930
assumptions to reimagine possibilities.

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:52.960
Pickup trucks haven’t changed much in appearance
for decades.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:56.509
Elon’s approach was to create something
entirely new.

00:01:56.509 --> 00:02:02.869
Once in every ten years, once in awhile, a
really special product comes along.

00:02:02.869 --> 00:02:05.329
We’ll remember those special moments.

00:02:05.329 --> 00:02:11.250
That people said was impossible and this is
one of those times.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:15.900
Despite how notoriously difficult the metal
is to work with, Elon was determined to create

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.900
a stainless steel vehicle.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:22.390
The Cybertruck will be heavy but a stainless
steel body can bear some of the load, enhancing

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:25.319
its durability and offering better protection
for passengers.

00:02:25.319 --> 00:02:32.440
If you’re ever in an argument with another
car, you will win.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:35.188
While the armor glass of the Cybertruck famously
cracked when struck by a steel ball a few

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:40.500
years ago, Elon is serious about the Cybertruck
being strong enough to withstand bullets

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:46.900
If Al Capone showed up with a Tommy gun and
emptied the entire magazine through the car

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.320
door, you’d still be alive.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:55.870
People said, ‘Why’d you make it bulletproof?’

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:58.810
I’m like, ‘Why not?’”

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:04.390
The Cybertruck uses a special type of cold-rolled
stainless steel patented by Tesla.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:10.420
Hot rolling involves heating steel to over
1,700 degrees Fahrenheit (927° Celsius),

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:12.390
making it soft and malleable.

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:15.230
The steel is pressed and shaped by big rollers.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:19.780
As it cools, it shrinks, causing the tiny
grains inside the steel that got stretched

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:22.500
out to relax back to their normal shape.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:26.810
This results in less precision in the size
and finish of the final product.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:30.930
While hot-rolled steel isn’t very strong,
it’s good enough for things like railroad

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:31.930
tracks.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:35.310
In cold rolling, the steel is cooled to room
temperature.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:39.890
Rolling this cooler, harder steel requires
significantly more force.

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:44.700
The intense pressure during this process makes
the steel thinner and longer.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:48.730
The grains inside the steel get stretched
out in the direction it’s rolled and don’t

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:50.860
revert back to their original state.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:55.800
This gives cold-rolled steel its superior
strength and a smoother finish.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:04:01.629
But cold-rolled steel is also harder to bend
and shape, so straight planes and sharp angles

00:04:01.629 --> 00:04:03.200
are more practical

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.220
You can’t actually stamp the body panels.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:09.510
The body panels would break the stamping machine.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:13.360
Stainless steel also doesn’t need to be
painted thanks to its natural rust resistance

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:15.840
which reduces manufacturing costs.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:20.370
When Franz von Holzhausen presented Elon with
a full-size mockup of the Cybertruck in July

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:24.210
2019, Elon’s immediate response was: “That’s
it!

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.210
I love it.

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:26.690
We are doing that.”

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:30.630
When some members of Tesla’s design team
suggested doing some market testing to see

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:35.229
how the public would receive it, Elon replied:
“I don’t do focus groups.”

00:04:35.229 --> 00:04:40.080
As reported in Isaacson’s book, Elon explained:
“I don’t care if no one buys it.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.230
We’re not doing a traditional boring truck.

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:43.850
We can always do that later.

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:46.010
I want to build something that’s cool.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:48.190
Like, don’t resist me.”

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:51.070
He pushed for a prototype in just three months.

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:55.910
The world got a taste of the Cybertruck in
November 2019 where Elon announced its expected

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:57.330
range and pricing.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:01.479
Fast forward three years later, when Tesla
delivered the first Cybertrucks in November

00:05:01.479 --> 00:05:02.759
2023.

00:05:02.759 --> 00:05:03.759
Thank you for buying a cybertruck

00:05:03.759 --> 00:05:09.130
However, the Cybertruck's range hasn't quite
met the targets initially set at its debut,

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:10.720
even with a range extender.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:13.360
Pricing has also increased.

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:18.130
Although people have been eagerly anticipating
the delivery of more Cybertrucks, Elon is

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:20.080
quick to temper expectations.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:25.800
At best, he expects 250,000 Cybertrucks a
year to come off the assembly lines beginning

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.550
in 2025.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:34.250
As the saying goes, good things take time,
and the Cybertruck is no ordinary vehicle.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:38.940
